{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4a573e7bfd1e047000fc3b0335a4fb147a9e64145b43ec960122d6393dbfdf03","digest":{"component_or_area":"comment-hygiene gate wiring","key_entities":["scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py","Makefile","lint target",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","tests/unit/test_comment_hygiene_guard.py","scripts/gen_env_registry.py","tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["comment hygiene","lint gate","local divergence","CI mismatch"],"propositions":["The comment-hygiene gate runs in CI as a standalone step but is not reachable via the local make lint target, causing the local verdict to diverge from CI's verdict.","Running make lint locally does not surface comment-hygiene failures that CI catches, leading to wasted review cycles when CI rejects trees that pass local checks.","The comment-hygiene gate must be wired into the make lint target alongside the gen_env_registry.py precedent to align local and CI behavior.","The standalone CI step in _build-and-test.yml must remain in place to maintain compatibility with patchsets predating the gate."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787871764729179001,"uuid":"70bf94c3-7634-4f80-91b0-82150d63d94b"}